Description: load the shader from /usr/share/eternalforest-by-soulman
 The packaged executable is the debug build, which reads the fragment shader
 at run time. Upstream runs unifdef in a shell to write gen/fshader-debug.glsl
 in the current directory, then loads it, and watches fshader.glsl in the
 current directory to reload it while editing. Load the installed shader
 directly (fshader.glsl has no #if blocks, so unifdef does not change it) and
 drop the file monitor: the demo no longer creates a gen/ directory where it
 is started, nor needs unifdef at run time.
